{
  "_doc": [
    "Per-class metadata that pipe_data_builder.py uses to construct each",
    "class's pipe-row table. Replaces the AI-generated `pipe_data` field.",
    "",
    "Schema:",
    "  • size_groups       — named arrays of NPS strings, referenced by class",
    "                        entries to avoid repeating 22-size lists 79 times",
    "  • classes[code]     — per-class entry:",
    "      .pipe_code       — exact string for the 'Code' row of the PMS",
    "      .sizes           — name from size_groups (or inline array if class-specific)",
    "      .transition_nps  — first NPS that flips from small_bore → large_bore.",
    "                          Sizes < transition_nps use small_bore values;",
    "                          sizes ≥ transition_nps use large_bore values.",
    "                          For classes with no transition (single pipe-type),",
    "                          set transition_nps to a value above the largest size.",
    "      .small_bore      — { pipe_type, material_spec } for sizes < transition_nps",
    "      .large_bore      — { pipe_type, material_spec } for sizes ≥ transition_nps",
    "      .ends            — typically 'BE' (bevel end), 'PE' (plain) for CuNi/tubing",
    "",
    "Engineering values (od_mm, schedule, wall_thickness_mm) are computed by",
    "pipe_data_builder.py at request time, not stored here:",
    "  • od_mm comes from pipe_dimensions.json (canonical ASME B36.10M)",
    "  • schedule + wall_thickness_mm come from dual-case Eq. 3a + project floor",
    "    (see pipe_data.correct_pipe_data and project_schedule_floors.json)",
    "",
    "Non-ASME classes (CuNi A30, Copper A40, GRE A50/51/52, CPVC A60, Titanium A70,",
    "Tubing T80*/T90*) carry explicit per-NPS od_mm/wall_thickness_mm tables since",
    "their dimensions don't follow ASME B36.10M. See the `non_asme_tables` block.",
    "",
    "When a new class is added: append it to `classes`, restart the server."
  ],

